WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:01.430
Eco-lodges.

2
00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:02.520
Green getaways.

3
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:06.910
Leaf-shaped labels promising
travel that cares for nature.

4
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.870
But a label can be used
without real change.

5
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.630
That's greenwashing.

6
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.810
The Galápagos Islands, Ecuador,
are a World Heritage Site.

7
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.540
UNESCO lists increased tourism
among their main threats.

8
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.870
Ecotourism crosses borders, but no
world body can enforce its rules.

9
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.510
So who keeps it honest?

10
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.570
Host governments?

11
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.670
A UN agency?

12
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.510
Paid-for certificates?

13
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.730
The tourists?

14
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:35.190
In this mission, you'll test
four international tools:

15
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:40.710
a declaration, a conference, a
certification scheme and a heritage list.

16
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.630
Then you'll see how the Galápagos
actually manages its visitors.

17
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.190
Your mission: decide who
really keeps ecotourism honest,

18
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.870
and explain why.
